@startuml
title UC06 - immutable result membership and cursor (REVIEW)
autonumber
actor "Reporting application" as C
participant "Report query service" as S
participant "Committed financial history" as L
participant "Query / snapshot members" as Q
C -> S : queryRequestId, X,Y, packageIds, OR/AND, includeFee, pageSize
S -> S : verify scope/caller/filters, default50 max200
S -> Q : resolve caller + queryRequestId / canonical filters
Q --> S : existing fixed query or new claim; different filters conflict
alt READY query already exists
 Q --> S : reuse original membership, totals and cutoff
else BUILDING query needs first successful freeze
 S -> Q : get or persist original cutoff, preserve on retry
 S -> L : one consistent source selection by recordedAt in [X,Y)\nusing original cutoff
 L --> S : committed qualifying ledger / subscriber membership
 S -> Q : persist fixed members + derived subscriber totals atomically
 Q --> S : durable READY query, caller/filter/version unchanged
end
S -> Q : first page ordered by subscriber
S --> C : queryId, fixed page, protected cursor
... new ledger becomes visible ...
C -> S : next cursor
S -> S : verify integrity/caller/filter/query/version
alt valid retained snapshot
 S -> Q : page from SAME persisted membership
 Q --> S : next members, no live membership changes
 S --> C : fixed next page / final page
else invalid/expired snapshot
 S --> C : reject / request new query, never substitute live result
end
note over L,Q
 recordedAt is business timestamp in ultimately committed tx.
 It is not physical COMMIT completion time.
 Page processing never holds an open DB transaction while user reads.
 OR: any selected package; AND: every selected package per subscriber.
end note
@enduml
